        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Thousands of students, workmen, citizens, and soldiers paraded along the Bund around the European quarter. They opened fire opposite the Victoria Hotel in the British Concession.",
            "block_bbox": [
                1084,
                1451,
                1992,
                1628
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1084.0,
                    1451.0
                ],
                [
                    1992.0,
                    1451.0
                ],
                [
                    1992.0,
                    1628.0
                ],
                [
                    1084.0,
                    1628.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "British and French Marines replied with machine guns. The firing lasted twenty minutes.",
            "block_bbox": [
                1069,
                1626,
                1960,
                1729
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1069.0,
                    1626.0
                ],
                [
                    1960.0,
                    1626.0
                ],
                [
                    1960.0,
                    1729.0
                ],
                [
                    1069.0,
                    1729.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A French merchant named Pasquier, and the Commissioner of Customs were killed. One British Marine and two civilians were wounded.",
            "block_bbox": [
                1070,
                1726,
                1924,
                1863
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1070.0,
                    1726.0
                ],
                [
                    1924.0,
                    1726.0
                ],
                [
                    1924.0,
                    1863.0
                ],
                [
                    1070.0,
                    1863.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "All the evidence indicates that the Chinese fired first. - Router.",
            "block_bbox": [
                1082,
                1856,
                1895,
                1927
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1082.0,
                    1856.0
                ],
                [
                    1895.0,
                    1856.0
                ],
                [
                    1895.0,
                    1927.0
                ],
                [
                    1082.0,
                    1927.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "EYEWITNESS'S STORY:- The report that the Chinese fired first is confirmed to a certain extent by the statement made to a \"China Mail\" representative this morning by the compradore of W. A. Hannibal & Co., who was one of the passengers on the Sai On which was alongside at the Canton side when the firing took place.",
            "block_bbox": [
                1080,
                1989,
                1935,
                2265
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1080.0,
                    1989.0
                ],
                [
                    1935.0,
                    1989.0
                ],
                [
                    1935.0,
                    2265.0
                ],
                [
                    1080.0,
                    2265.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "\"I saw many schoolboys and workmen marching along the Bund about half past two yesterday a afternoon,\" he said. \"And when they had got about half way past Shameen they fired shots across to the Shameen side, The fire was returned. Rain came down heavily about the same time and I saw the people running but very little else. The Sat On remained alongside for many hours and I saw foreigners leaving Shameen for the gunboats.\"",
            "block_bbox": [
                1079,
                2265,
                1962,
                2638
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1079.0,
                    2265.0
                ],
                [
                    1962.0,
                    2265.0
                ],
                [
                    1962.0,
                    2638.0
                ],
                [
                    1079.0,
                    2638.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The \"China Mail\" informant said that his information had been first that twenty Chinese had been killed as a result of the fire from Shameen and then, that fifty had been killed. It was impossible to ascertain anything definite in this respect as the Sal On had its own difficulties to contend with, the seamen having left to attend a meeting on shore at which they were to be told with or not they would be allowed to man the ship to bring it back to Hongkong. The crow returned and said that they were to be allowed to make the trip. The ship left about 7 p.m. and arrived in Hongkong early this morning.",
            "block_bbox": [
                1077,
                2637,
                1987,
                3145
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1077.0,
                    2637.0
                ],
                [
                    1987.0,
                    2637.0
                ],
                [
                    1987.0,
                    3145.0
                ],
                [
                    1077.0,
                    3145.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A man in a sampan who was making for the\nSai On from Skamoen was killed when within\na few feet of the boat, according to our\ninformant, who added that as the boat\npassed Honam about 8 p.m. he observed\nsoldiers of Gonoral Li Fook-lam's army\nleaving Honam for Canton",
            "block_bbox": [
                1086,
                3147,
                1976,
                3390
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1086.0,
                    3147.0
                ],
                [
                    1976.0,
                    3147.0
                ],
                [
                    1976.0,
                    3390.0
                ],
                [
                    1086.0,
                    3390.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "PANIC OF GROWDS. - So fast-the-rumour that a detachment of the East Surrcys is to leave Hongkong for Canton today is not confirmed officially, but it is significant that the s.s. Paul Boau which arrived in Hongkong early this morning, from Canton, is now lying off Stonecutter's Island, and that the Sa'on, also from Canton, is under orders to leave for the same port. At present the Sa'on is alongside the wharf and",
            "block_bbox": [
                1086,
                3410,
                1966,
                3762
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    1086.0,
                    3410.0
                ],
                [
                    1966.0,
                    3410.0
                ],
                [
                    1966.0,
                    3762.0
                ],
                [
                    1086.0,
                    3762.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Mr. Edwards was wounded, not killed. -\nRouter.",
            "block_bbox": [
                2031,
                1457,
                2773,
                1542
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 12,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    2031.0,
                    1457.0
                ],
                [
                    2773.0,
                    1457.0
                ],
                [
                    2773.0,
                    1542.0
                ],
                [
                    2031.0,
                    1542.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "refugees are still swarming the vicinity. The crowds which have come down from Canton are said to be as large as those going to that city. The crowds on the wharf at present seem puzzled what to do. They drift on and off the ships according to whether or not it is raining at the time. They all appear to be soaked through and to be roam disconsolate. A guard of Volunteers is on duty at the wharves. A West River stoomer appears to be the only boat that will leave today for the \"China Mail\" understands that no ships will leave for Canton for the present. The vessels tied up here, it is stated, will be used to house European refugees from Sha'meon arriving by the s.s. Honam in large number this afternoon. The Honam is reported to have been manned by naval ratings. The refugees are said to number 600 -- though one report puts the figure at 1,500. The wounded are aboard, it is added and the ambulance will meet the vessel here.",
            "block_bbox": [
                2018,
                1597,
                2894,
                2414
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 13,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    2018.0,
